WEBVTT

00:01:24.140 --> 00:01:26.770
<i>The year is 1889.</i>

00:01:27.190 --> 00:01:30.060
<i>The crew members on board the Nautilus make a landing on Atlantis</i>

00:01:30.060 --> 00:01:31.940
<i>to bury comrades fallen in battle.</i>

00:01:31.940 --> 00:01:36.570
<i>At the burial grounds, Jean learns his father was killed by a Garfish.</i>

00:01:37.110 --> 00:01:38.910
<i>Suppressing his grief within his breast,</i>

00:01:38.910 --> 00:01:41.700
<i>Jean boards the Nautilus for her new journey.</i>

00:01:46.410 --> 00:01:48.830
One, two, three...

00:01:48.830 --> 00:01:51.380
Four, five, six...

00:02:17.990 --> 00:02:19.950
I'm sorry.

00:02:21.620 --> 00:02:26.250
Now look here, Miss Grandis! What do you think you're doing?

00:02:26.250 --> 00:02:28.750
Are you blind? I'm having my tea.

00:02:28.750 --> 00:02:33.290
As long as you are on this ship, you will follow the rules.

00:02:35.670 --> 00:02:39.760
I'm too mature to engage in such childish exercises.

00:02:39.760 --> 00:02:42.430
I'm only interested in beauty exercises.

00:02:42.430 --> 00:02:49.270
I can understand. So much weight must make exercise most tiring.

00:02:49.270 --> 00:02:54.980
In spite of all your exercising, your waistline isn't too slim.

00:02:55.980 --> 00:02:57.440
What did you say?

00:02:57.440 --> 00:02:59.240
Do you want to start something?

00:03:02.530 --> 00:03:08.040
One, two, three, four, five, six...

00:03:09.660 --> 00:03:13.380
It feels good to exercise like this out on the deck.

00:03:13.380 --> 00:03:17.760
Yeah, it was cramped inside the submarine.

00:03:18.380 --> 00:03:20.880
You don't seem to complain as much as you used to.

00:03:20.880 --> 00:03:25.010
Really? I guess I'm getting used to life aboard this ship.

00:03:25.010 --> 00:03:28.470
But we still get nothing but fish for meals.

00:03:28.470 --> 00:03:30.440
I've gotten used to that too.

00:03:30.980 --> 00:03:36.690
You used to complain about earaches when the ship dived.

00:03:36.690 --> 00:03:38.940
Not anymore.

00:03:46.910 --> 00:03:48.870
Nadia seems like her old self again.

00:03:48.870 --> 00:03:50.910
Right, she's a kid again.

00:03:52.670 --> 00:03:54.250
By the way, Hanson...

00:03:54.250 --> 00:03:54.960
What?

00:03:55.540 --> 00:03:56.670
About Electra...

00:03:57.300 --> 00:03:59.460
What about Electra?

00:03:59.960 --> 00:04:03.590
I'll tell you how you can get closer to her.

00:04:03.590 --> 00:04:04.680
But...

00:04:04.680 --> 00:04:07.850
I've got years of experience in this kind of thing.

00:04:07.850 --> 00:04:09.890
The best strategy is to attack!

00:04:10.480 --> 00:04:13.230
Attack? I don't like that.

00:04:13.480 --> 00:04:16.860
Unless you try, you'll never find out.

00:04:16.860 --> 00:04:19.780
Love must be approached positively, actively!

00:04:19.780 --> 00:04:23.950
A do or die spirit will lead you to victory!

00:04:23.950 --> 00:04:27.240
Never rest in your efforts until you succeed!

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:31.660
How do I start?

00:04:32.370 --> 00:04:33.120
With flowers!

00:04:34.870 --> 00:04:35.540
Flowers?

00:04:35.540 --> 00:04:38.500
That's right. Flowers break down a girl's resistance.

00:04:39.550 --> 00:04:43.220
But there aren't any flowers at all aboard this ship.

00:04:43.220 --> 00:04:45.180
Then you have to make some.

00:04:45.760 --> 00:04:46.640
Make some?

00:04:46.640 --> 00:04:50.560
That's right! Make them with your own hands.

00:04:57.400 --> 00:04:58.520
Hey, Jean!

00:04:59.570 --> 00:05:01.030
Eiko?

00:05:01.440 --> 00:05:04.650
I was wondering whether you wanted to join our fan club.

00:05:04.900 --> 00:05:05.990
Fan club?

00:05:05.990 --> 00:05:09.330
Yes, a fan club for our nurse, Miss Ikorina.

00:05:09.780 --> 00:05:12.790
If you join now, you get a photo like this

00:05:12.790 --> 00:05:15.120
with your membership card.

00:05:15.410 --> 00:05:16.830
Who are the members?

00:05:21.800 --> 00:05:23.380
She certainly is popular.

00:05:23.380 --> 00:05:25.090
Will you join?

00:05:25.090 --> 00:05:27.050
I'd like to, but...

00:05:27.470 --> 00:05:28.890
But what?

00:05:29.550 --> 00:05:31.350
I have Nadia.

00:05:33.020 --> 00:05:33.810
So what?

00:05:33.810 --> 00:05:37.650
I don't think it's right to think about two girls at the same time.

00:05:39.900 --> 00:05:43.320
Listen to me, Jean. I'm going to give you some good advice.

00:05:44.150 --> 00:05:45.240
That is that,

00:05:46.030 --> 00:05:47.110
and this is this!

00:05:48.110 --> 00:05:49.320
Is that so?

00:05:52.200 --> 00:05:54.120
I guess you're still a kid.

00:05:54.500 --> 00:05:55.830
I am not a kid!

00:05:56.120 --> 00:05:57.670
Look at yourselves!

00:05:57.670 --> 00:05:59.630
You're too old to be concerned with a fan club!

00:05:59.630 --> 00:06:02.460
At any rate, I'm not joining!

00:06:02.460 --> 00:06:02.880
Bye!

00:06:05.170 --> 00:06:06.760
Poor Jean.

00:06:08.090 --> 00:06:13.350
Since leaving Atlantis, everyone seems more friendly.

00:06:13.560 --> 00:06:16.850
They're just sympathizing with us.

00:06:16.850 --> 00:06:17.850
I wonder.

00:06:17.850 --> 00:06:20.770
Of course, grown-ups always act like that.

00:06:20.770 --> 00:06:24.730
Grown-ups? They all treat me like a child.

00:06:24.730 --> 00:06:25.940
Well, aren't you?

00:06:26.400 --> 00:06:30.160
You're wrong! There are certain things I've decided for myself.

00:06:31.030 --> 00:06:32.070
What things?

00:06:32.410 --> 00:06:34.040
Well, for one thing...

00:06:34.040 --> 00:06:35.490
Found you!

00:06:37.200 --> 00:06:39.500
Now it's Jean's turn to be It.

00:06:39.500 --> 00:06:40.330
Darn it!

00:06:40.330 --> 00:06:41.630
Hurry!

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:43.670
Okay, Marie.

00:06:43.670 --> 00:06:45.420
Hurry, King, over here.

00:06:46.630 --> 00:06:48.470
Are you ready?

00:06:48.470 --> 00:06:50.510
No, not yet!

00:06:51.970 --> 00:06:54.510
How can he claim to be grown-up when he acts like that?

00:06:56.970 --> 00:06:57.930
What is it?

00:06:58.390 --> 00:07:01.650
Well, I have a request.

00:07:03.020 --> 00:07:06.980
I want to become a full-fledged member of the crew.

00:07:06.980 --> 00:07:09.700
I want to avenge the death of my father.

00:07:09.700 --> 00:07:12.030
Please, Captain Nemo!

00:07:12.660 --> 00:07:14.120
I cannot allow that.

00:07:14.580 --> 00:07:16.620
Is it because I'm too young?

00:07:17.910 --> 00:07:20.080
It's because you cannot kill anyone.

00:07:21.790 --> 00:07:25.210
Jean, the reason we're fighting

00:07:25.210 --> 00:07:28.510
is to create a world where people like you don't have to kill.

00:07:29.220 --> 00:07:33.720
We don't want you to dirty your hands. Can you understand that?

00:07:33.720 --> 00:07:35.890
Yes, I understand.

00:07:39.140 --> 00:07:41.560
I have a request.

00:07:42.560 --> 00:07:47.530
That's why I want you to persuade Captain Nemo.

00:07:47.530 --> 00:07:49.150
I can't do that.

00:07:50.280 --> 00:07:51.110
But...

00:07:51.450 --> 00:07:53.700
It's exactly like Captain Nemo told you.

00:07:55.660 --> 00:07:57.450
It's no use.

00:07:57.450 --> 00:07:59.750
I understand.

00:08:01.830 --> 00:08:02.870
What is it?

00:08:03.370 --> 00:08:05.420
Well, I have a request.

00:08:08.300 --> 00:08:10.170
You really mean that?

00:08:10.720 --> 00:08:14.590
I made the same request directly to Captain Nemo and to Miss Electra.

00:08:15.050 --> 00:08:17.050
And what did they say?

00:08:19.020 --> 00:08:20.020
They said no.

00:08:20.560 --> 00:08:22.230
That's what I thought.

00:08:22.520 --> 00:08:26.190
But I just have to become a member of the crew.

00:08:26.190 --> 00:08:28.610
Can't you help me?

00:08:28.610 --> 00:08:30.690
There's nothing we can do.

00:08:30.690 --> 00:08:34.660
Jean, aren't you asking the wrong people to help you?

00:08:35.570 --> 00:08:37.830
If you really feel that way,

00:08:37.830 --> 00:08:42.330
you have to keep pressing Captain Nemo and Electra to accept you.

00:08:42.620 --> 00:08:45.540
Why do you rely on others? Do it yourself.

00:08:47.040 --> 00:08:48.840
A child relies on others,

00:08:48.840 --> 00:08:52.970
but a man takes care of such things himself.

00:09:04.270 --> 00:09:06.770
Don't rely on others. Do it yourself.

00:09:12.400 --> 00:09:12.940
Jean...

00:09:13.490 --> 00:09:14.280
Oh, Nadia.

00:09:16.860 --> 00:09:18.990
What are you looking so glum about?

00:09:18.990 --> 00:09:22.120
I'm not. Did you want something?

00:09:23.540 --> 00:09:25.080
Oh, nothing in particular.

00:09:25.920 --> 00:09:29.670
The sky is dazzling, but beautiful.

00:09:32.380 --> 00:09:35.880
Say, Jean, don't you want to fly through the skies again?

00:09:38.260 --> 00:09:40.850
I'd like to fly again

00:09:41.640 --> 00:09:43.560
in an airplane built by Jean.

00:09:45.390 --> 00:09:46.520
Of course we can!

00:09:47.100 --> 00:09:49.650
I'll build another aircraft!

00:09:49.650 --> 00:09:52.320
There's an idea I've got for a new design.

00:09:52.320 --> 00:09:54.570
We'll fly through the skies again.

00:09:55.320 --> 00:09:56.860
That's wonderful!

00:09:57.150 --> 00:09:59.950
All right! I'll start right away!

00:10:00.240 --> 00:10:02.240
Right! Good luck!

00:10:09.830 --> 00:10:13.300
What in the world has Jean started now?

00:10:13.300 --> 00:10:16.010
He's designing another airplane.

00:10:16.010 --> 00:10:18.130
And Nadia?

00:10:18.510 --> 00:10:20.140
She's with Jean.

00:10:22.640 --> 00:10:24.140
Marie wins!

00:10:24.140 --> 00:10:27.270
Everyone seems to be bitten by a love bug.

00:10:29.560 --> 00:10:31.810
Jean, I'm coming in.

00:10:34.320 --> 00:10:38.070
What is all this? There's no room to stand.

00:10:38.070 --> 00:10:39.280
There's space over there.

00:10:40.490 --> 00:10:42.160
You mean there?

00:10:42.870 --> 00:10:46.160
Geez! When are you going to eat?

00:10:46.160 --> 00:10:48.120
Everyone else finished long ago.

00:10:48.120 --> 00:10:52.080
Sorry, I was just too busy.

00:10:52.080 --> 00:10:54.170
Are you going to eat or not?

00:10:54.670 --> 00:10:57.970
Leave it in the mess hall. I'll eat it later.

00:10:58.260 --> 00:11:00.720
Do as you please!

00:11:00.720 --> 00:11:01.800
Nadia...

00:11:02.300 --> 00:11:06.220
It won't be long before I can take you up into the skies again.

00:11:06.560 --> 00:11:08.060
Okay.

00:11:28.540 --> 00:11:31.080
There, they're finished!

00:11:31.500 --> 00:11:34.590
Look, they're finished, Sanson. I just have to wait for them to dry.

00:11:34.590 --> 00:11:38.260
So you've made flowers. Good for you.

00:11:39.130 --> 00:11:42.180
I guess I'll go and see how Jean is doing.

00:11:42.720 --> 00:11:45.350
Gosh, this is hard.

00:11:46.010 --> 00:11:49.230
The problem is this variable equipment.

00:11:49.770 --> 00:11:51.310
Hey, how's it going?

00:11:52.140 --> 00:11:52.900
Hanson!

00:11:53.350 --> 00:11:55.610
I just came to see how you were doing.

00:11:55.610 --> 00:11:58.730
You seem to be having some trouble.

00:11:59.320 --> 00:12:00.690
It's nothing to worry about.

00:12:00.690 --> 00:12:05.200
Don't be so touchy. I'll be glad to give you a hand.

00:12:05.200 --> 00:12:07.990
No thanks! I'll work it out by myself!

00:12:07.990 --> 00:12:11.910
Now, now, it's childish to be peevish like that.

00:12:12.460 --> 00:12:14.250
I'm not peevish!

00:12:14.250 --> 00:12:18.090
A child should be ready to take advice from grown-ups.

00:12:18.090 --> 00:12:20.210
That's what we're here for.

00:12:21.840 --> 00:12:26.180
I don't need help, and I'm not a child.

00:12:27.930 --> 00:12:29.600
You're over-reaching yourself.

00:12:29.970 --> 00:12:31.850
He's at that difficult age.

00:12:32.480 --> 00:12:33.310
Is that so?

00:12:33.850 --> 00:12:36.610
It happens all the time with boys.

00:12:36.610 --> 00:12:39.940
They're trying to go from boyhood to manhood.

00:12:40.730 --> 00:12:42.650
Why do they want to become adults?

00:12:42.990 --> 00:12:45.240
Because they can't continue otherwise.

00:12:46.070 --> 00:12:48.200
Why can't they continue?

00:12:48.200 --> 00:12:51.290
Because it takes an adult to win over another adult.

00:12:53.120 --> 00:12:56.460
It will happen to you as you get older too.

00:12:56.460 --> 00:12:57.920
Like you, Auntie?

00:12:57.920 --> 00:13:02.670
Don't call me Auntie! It fits someone like Electra more!

00:13:06.260 --> 00:13:09.470
But Jean hardly ever seems to come out of his room.

00:13:09.470 --> 00:13:13.430
Yeah, that's why Nadia is so mad all the time.

00:13:13.770 --> 00:13:15.770
That's not so!

00:13:16.190 --> 00:13:17.650
We understand.

00:13:17.650 --> 00:13:20.110
Really, it's not that way at all.

00:13:20.980 --> 00:13:26.160
Young as he is, he's already more interested in work than in a girl.

00:13:26.160 --> 00:13:27.950
I can see trying days ahead for you.

00:13:27.950 --> 00:13:29.660
You've got it all wrong!

00:13:30.950 --> 00:13:32.120
I wonder...

00:13:34.620 --> 00:13:36.580
Gosh, I'm hungry.

00:13:37.080 --> 00:13:40.250
Is there anything to eat?

00:13:40.250 --> 00:13:42.420
What time do you think it is now?

00:13:42.420 --> 00:13:45.880
I guess Miss Grandis has gone to bed already.

00:13:46.180 --> 00:13:50.220
If you're hungry, just make something yourself.

00:13:50.930 --> 00:13:53.680
I can't. I don't know how.

00:13:53.680 --> 00:13:54.560
What?

00:13:54.560 --> 00:13:57.980
My aunt always fed me.

00:13:58.440 --> 00:14:01.150
Meals are always prepared for you, right?

00:14:03.030 --> 00:14:06.490
Gosh, you have lived a very sheltered life.

00:14:06.950 --> 00:14:08.660
Are you criticizing me?

00:14:09.780 --> 00:14:11.870
No, just envious.

00:14:12.580 --> 00:14:14.580
Ever since we were kids,

00:14:14.580 --> 00:14:18.500
Sanson and I had to get everything for ourselves.

00:14:19.380 --> 00:14:22.000
Our food, our clothing.

00:14:23.090 --> 00:14:24.550
Do you know why?

00:14:25.760 --> 00:14:28.720
Otherwise we would have starved and died.

00:14:30.180 --> 00:14:35.680
Jean, you're big enough. Go and get something to eat for yourself!

00:14:45.230 --> 00:14:47.950
I certainly acted out of character.

00:14:50.910 --> 00:14:52.990
What's up at this time of night?

00:14:58.120 --> 00:15:00.460
Now I see.

00:15:00.830 --> 00:15:03.090
Oh, geez!

00:15:04.800 --> 00:15:11.840
These are just paper trash compared to your beauty, but my shy heart

00:15:13.220 --> 00:15:14.810
would like to present them to you.

00:15:16.640 --> 00:15:18.310
Wow...

00:15:18.730 --> 00:15:20.190
Sanson!

00:15:21.100 --> 00:15:23.610
Those flowers are the ones I made!

00:15:23.610 --> 00:15:29.570
Well, you see, I was just checking to see how they would work!

00:15:29.900 --> 00:15:32.030
Just checking?

00:15:32.030 --> 00:15:35.700
No, I didn't mean it that way!

00:15:38.410 --> 00:15:41.420
No! Wait, stop! Now calm down! Calm down!

00:15:47.300 --> 00:15:50.130
Hey! What's all this ruckus?

00:15:51.340 --> 00:15:55.970
I see. You're bothering my granddaughter again.

00:15:55.970 --> 00:15:59.850
Okay, show me your injuries!
I'll take care of them!

00:16:03.810 --> 00:16:05.810
This is pretty bad.

00:16:06.230 --> 00:16:07.190
What happened?

00:16:07.190 --> 00:16:08.900
I don't know.

00:16:11.780 --> 00:16:12.910
Where are you going?

00:16:13.860 --> 00:16:16.780
You prepared that food to take to Jean, didn't you?

00:16:16.780 --> 00:16:19.580
That's because Nadia likes Jean!

00:16:19.580 --> 00:16:21.210
You're wrong.

00:16:21.790 --> 00:16:24.250
No use hiding it. I know.

00:16:24.250 --> 00:16:28.750
People in love want to be together as much as possible!

00:16:29.090 --> 00:16:32.470
Marie, where did you learn such a thing?

00:16:32.720 --> 00:16:33.930
From Miss Grandis!

00:16:37.680 --> 00:16:42.270
That woman! She's always up to something bad!

00:16:46.230 --> 00:16:47.980
I wonder where he's going?

00:16:54.400 --> 00:16:54.950
Jean!

00:16:56.110 --> 00:16:57.070
Nadia...

00:16:57.780 --> 00:17:01.620
I couldn't find you, but here you are.

00:17:01.620 --> 00:17:05.120
Yes, when I have a difficult problem, I come here to think.

00:17:05.120 --> 00:17:08.670
It's like you to feel more at ease beside some machinery.

00:17:08.670 --> 00:17:09.670
Is that so?

00:17:09.670 --> 00:17:12.050
Ah, yes. Here's a snack.

00:17:15.010 --> 00:17:16.260
What's this?

00:17:16.260 --> 00:17:20.350
How rude! I spent so much time preparing that food!

00:17:20.350 --> 00:17:24.060
I see. Thanks!

00:17:24.640 --> 00:17:25.890
Eat it all up!

00:17:31.860 --> 00:17:33.780
What is this?

00:17:34.400 --> 00:17:36.450
The main engine.

00:17:36.450 --> 00:17:37.530
This thing?

00:17:37.530 --> 00:17:40.240
Yes, it's called a particle annihilation engine.

00:17:41.160 --> 00:17:42.200
What's that?

00:17:42.200 --> 00:17:44.120
I don't understand it myself.

00:17:44.120 --> 00:17:48.210
It's more advanced than anything known to 19th century science.

00:17:48.210 --> 00:17:50.170
Far beyond me.

00:17:51.500 --> 00:17:52.630
It sounds impressive.

00:17:53.670 --> 00:17:58.590
Today this is used only as a power source to kill people.

00:17:59.550 --> 00:18:02.470
Captain Nemo told me that himself.

00:18:02.470 --> 00:18:06.730
It's sad, but that's the world of grown-ups.

00:18:09.060 --> 00:18:11.770
I don't want to become an adult.

00:18:12.150 --> 00:18:13.980
I do, as soon as I can.

00:18:13.980 --> 00:18:15.440
Jean!

00:18:16.070 --> 00:18:18.740
For a child, dreams are very hard to realize.

00:18:18.740 --> 00:18:20.280
We can only chase after them.

00:18:21.200 --> 00:18:25.410
When I become an adult, I may be able to make my dreams come true.

00:18:26.120 --> 00:18:30.380
That's why I want to grow up, to realize my dreams.

00:18:30.630 --> 00:18:32.340
These are for you.

00:18:32.340 --> 00:18:35.630
How pretty! For me?

00:18:35.630 --> 00:18:39.380
Yes! It was hard to get the right coloring.

00:18:39.380 --> 00:18:41.140
You made these?

00:18:41.140 --> 00:18:41.970
Yes...

00:18:41.970 --> 00:18:46.060
Thank you! It will brighten up my room.

00:18:46.390 --> 00:18:49.020
Well, you...

00:18:49.020 --> 00:18:53.110
I know! I'll give some to Captain Nemo. Would that be all right?

00:18:53.320 --> 00:18:54.320
What?

00:18:54.320 --> 00:18:58.360
You see, he actually loves flowers very much.

00:18:58.360 --> 00:19:00.410
Is that so?

00:19:01.370 --> 00:19:03.620
Then please, give some to him.

00:19:06.450 --> 00:19:09.580
And then you walked away without saying anything?

00:19:09.580 --> 00:19:10.250
Yeah...

00:19:10.250 --> 00:19:14.710
What a fool! What happened to your do or die spirit?

00:19:16.000 --> 00:19:17.420
It doesn't matter.

00:19:18.970 --> 00:19:22.840
I don't like being in a do or die situation.

00:19:24.890 --> 00:19:30.060
You may call me a coward, but I'd rather wait.

00:19:33.270 --> 00:19:37.150
The problem is here, in the variable unit.

00:19:39.070 --> 00:19:41.320
What shall I do now?

00:19:41.990 --> 00:19:43.740
I can't figure it out.

00:19:43.740 --> 00:19:45.830
Looks like you need some help.

00:19:45.830 --> 00:19:48.290
I want to fly through the skies again.

00:19:48.290 --> 00:19:51.250
A child should rely on help from grown-ups.

00:19:52.460 --> 00:19:54.540
A child?

00:19:55.960 --> 00:19:57.500
Right! I've made up my mind!

00:19:57.500 --> 00:19:58.510
What's up?

00:19:58.510 --> 00:20:03.220
There's something I want to ask, Hanson.

00:20:04.220 --> 00:20:06.300
Of course.

00:20:06.300 --> 00:20:09.060
But you should have come to me earlier.

00:20:09.060 --> 00:20:11.810
Don't say that!

00:20:12.600 --> 00:20:15.810
Here, it's this variable unit.

00:20:15.810 --> 00:20:18.020
Okay, okay. Show me where.

00:20:18.690 --> 00:20:22.950
Here? Why don't you trying changing the shape of the cam?

00:20:22.950 --> 00:20:23.160
You're almost a man if you can realize what you can and can't do.

00:20:23.160 --> 00:20:25.370
I see! You're right!

00:20:25.370 --> 00:20:27.950
And do it this way over here.

00:20:27.950 --> 00:20:29.580
I follow you.

00:20:40.170 --> 00:20:41.630
You've done it, Jean!

00:20:41.630 --> 00:20:43.130
Yeah, thanks.

00:20:43.130 --> 00:20:47.850
This aircraft has no balloon or wings. Will it really fly?

00:20:47.850 --> 00:20:50.600
Don't worry. The theory behind it is perfect.

00:20:51.180 --> 00:20:53.440
It won't be another failure?

00:20:53.440 --> 00:20:57.770
Don't worry. This time I had help building it.

00:20:58.770 --> 00:21:00.730
Marie wants to fly too.

00:21:00.730 --> 00:21:04.200
Now, now, let those two be alone for a while.

00:21:04.200 --> 00:21:06.490
You mean like a married couple?

00:21:06.490 --> 00:21:07.490
That's right.

00:21:07.820 --> 00:21:08.950
Come on, get in.

00:21:09.330 --> 00:21:10.410
All right.

00:21:17.250 --> 00:21:18.790
Revving the power up.

00:21:19.090 --> 00:21:20.090
Ready for take-off!

00:21:23.130 --> 00:21:24.380
Is it safe?

00:21:24.380 --> 00:21:26.300
Don't worry. Here we go!

00:21:33.890 --> 00:21:35.020
Jean, what's wrong?

00:21:35.020 --> 00:21:35.560
Lift off!

00:21:37.020 --> 00:21:39.110
Jean, you can do it!

00:21:43.610 --> 00:21:44.490
Fly!

00:21:46.450 --> 00:21:48.160
Jean, take off!

00:21:49.660 --> 00:21:51.370
Jean, you can do it!

00:21:52.910 --> 00:21:55.540
Fly!

00:22:00.960 --> 00:22:02.590
It's flying!

00:22:02.590 --> 00:22:03.510
It's in the air!

00:22:03.670 --> 00:22:04.380
Go!

00:22:12.220 --> 00:22:14.180
We made it! We made it!

00:22:14.180 --> 00:22:15.890
We're flying! We're really flying!

00:22:16.390 --> 00:22:18.100
See, Nadia? We're flying!

00:22:18.690 --> 00:22:21.310
Yes, you're really a genius!

00:22:26.700 --> 00:22:29.570
He's a remarkable kid.

00:22:30.490 --> 00:22:32.620
He's become a man.

00:22:34.160 --> 00:22:36.160
You did it, Jean.

00:22:46.170 --> 00:22:49.680
Wow! It feels so good!

00:22:50.010 --> 00:22:52.640
I've never seen clouds this close before.

00:22:53.050 --> 00:22:55.180
I can almost grab some!

00:22:56.810 --> 00:22:58.390
Shall we go into the clouds?

00:23:01.560 --> 00:23:03.150
I can't see anything!

00:23:03.270 --> 00:23:05.030
Nothing to worry about!

00:23:07.400 --> 00:23:08.570
Say, Nadia.

00:23:08.570 --> 00:23:09.530
What?

00:23:09.530 --> 00:23:10.950
One thing is clear to me now.

00:23:10.950 --> 00:23:12.410
What is it?

00:23:13.620 --> 00:23:15.410
The difference between the Jean I used to be,

00:23:15.410 --> 00:23:16.870
and the Jean I'll be from today.

00:23:18.750 --> 00:23:22.250
I'm going to stay on this ship and study.

00:23:22.250 --> 00:23:27.210
Not only science, but also about life and the world of adults.

00:23:27.210 --> 00:23:31.760
Now we're just flying through the sky, so this won't take you there.

00:23:32.470 --> 00:23:36.220
But if I grow up and become a man who can look after you,

00:23:37.140 --> 00:23:38.930
I promise to take you to Africa!

00:23:43.440 --> 00:23:44.900
I'll be waiting!
